  "_comment": "Time zones of the US pack: a curated dataset (CC BY 4.0, see datasets/LICENSE.md). packbuild.timezones turns it into the usa pack's `timezones` polygon layer, which answers for points in the United States before the world pack's coarser layer. `admin1` has one entry per feature of the pack's states layer (iso:US-XX): an IANA zone for a state with one zone, or an object with `zone` (the rest of the state) and `parts` (counties, census:<GEOID> -> zone). A zone can be a list: the county is split along a line the pack doesn't draw; the first entry is its main zone and the nearest town inside it whose zone is listed decides. `shapes` take precedence: Census AIANNH areas (`aiannh`: the AIANNHCE code) or boxes [south, west, north, east]. Every zone must exist in the tz database; `sources` name entries of the top-level `sources`.",
